# Images and archives are binary everywhere in this repository.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.zip       binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payload protection -- KEEP THIS BLOCK LAST.
#
# The package identifies every file it manages by checksum. A payload whose
# bytes are rewritten in transit -- line-ending conversion above all -- will
# never match its declared hash, so a correctly authored rule reports as
# blocked forever, for a reason nothing in the tool can show the operator.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both directions while leaving the
# files diffable, so a vendor's CRLF file stays CRLF and a file shipped with no
# trailing newline keeps having none.
#
# The patterns MUST keep the leading `**/`. A pattern containing a slash is
# anchored to this file's directory, so a bare `payload/**` protects only a
# top-level folder and silently misses every other depth -- including
# administrator/components/com_ecskccustom/payload/ and anything the build
# copies. Measured, not assumed: under core.autocrlf=true the nested copy of a
# CRLF file was stored as LF while the top-level copy kept its CRLF.
#
# Both spellings are covered while the canonical folder name is unsettled --
# the brief says `payloads/` (decision 17, section 6) and section 5.6 says
# `payload/`. Drop the unused line once that is decided.
#
# Git applies the LAST matching pattern, so any general rule added below this
# block would silently override it. Add new rules above, not here.
#
# See the project brief -- decision 17, and the first pitfall in section 6.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/payload/**   -text
**/payloads/**  -text
